{"parentUuid":"a4b21614-718f-4000-85c2-3960217f4ab9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1ec9ed76-4982-4973-85e2-3f6d3abc155e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Briefing: Per-agent live streaming for entire review\n\n  Background\n\n  PR #1184 (just merged-or-pending) fixed the drill-in viewport for entire review multi-agent runs. One issue\n  explicitly deferred from that PR: each agent buffers its stdout until completion, so the drill-in event buffer\n  fills in one burst at end-of-run instead of streaming as the agent works. We labeled this \"PR B\" in the\n  brainstorm.\n\n  Current behavior (the problem)\n\n  - RunMulti (cmd/entire/cli/review/run_multi.go) fans events from per-agent goroutines into a single dispatch loop\n  - The TUI sink (tui_sink.go) is ready to display events as they arrive — AgentEvent is called per event, dispatch\n  is already serialized\n  - The bottleneck is upstream: each agent's reviewer/parser doesn't emit AssistantText / ToolCall events until the\n  agent process exits, because each adapter waits for the full stdout before parsing\n  - User-visible symptom: drill-in shows \"(0 events)\" until the agent finishes, then jumps to \"(N events)\" all at\n  once\n\n  Target behavior\n\n  Each agent emits events incrementally as stdout arrives. Drill-in shows live progress; dashboard preview column\n  updates in real time.\n\n  Key files\n\n  - Shared scaffolding: cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go — ReviewerTemplate (Spawn → pipe stdout → run parser\n   → forward events → close). Each agent supplies BuildCmd and Parser.\n  - Per-agent reviewers (each has its own parser):\n    - cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go — Claude Code uses stream-json output, should be line-by-line\n  already; verify why events arrive batched\n    - cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer.go — Codex includes filterCodexOutput chrome filter; check if filter\n  buffers before emit\n    - cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/reviewer.go — Gemini CLI parser\n  - Event types: cmd/entire/cli/review/types/event.go — AssistantText, ToolCall, RunError, RunFinished\n  - Sinks: cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_sink.go, dump.go, synthesis_sink.go — all already handle per-event dispatch\n\n  Investigation starting points\n\n  1. Add a debug log in Run's event forwarding loop (or in ReviewerTemplate's pipe goroutine) printing time.Now() +\n  event kind. Run a real review and check whether events arrive at staggered timestamps or all at once.\n  2. If they're staggered at the template level but show up batched in the TUI → the issue is in TUI rendering or\n  sink dispatch.\n  3. If they're batched at the template level → check each parser: are they using bufio.Scanner (line-by-line, OK)\n  or reading full stdout (batched, BAD)?\n  4. Specifically suspect Codex — filterCodexOutput may collect chrome-filtered output before forwarding.\n\n  Constraints (do NOT break)\n\n  - Serial-dispatch contract: RunMulti already serializes events through a single dispatch loop. Don't move to\n  per-sink goroutines.\n  - RunFinished blocks on TUI dismissal: don't change the order of RunFinished vs sink writes.\n  - Cancellation: events arriving after ctx.Done() should still flush (we want partial output preserved on Ctrl+C).\n  - tea.Program.Send thread safety: the TUI's Send is goroutine-safe per Bubble Tea, but the sink relies on dispatch\n   serialization — keep that.\n\n  Smoke test\n\n  After implementing, run entire review with at least two agents configured (claude-code + codex). In the drill-in\n  (Ctrl+O during the run), the event buffer should grow visibly while the agent is still working. Compare against\n  the current behavior (drill-in is empty until end).\n\n  Anti-features (don't add)\n\n  - Don't add a throttle / debounce layer — let events flow as they arrive\n  - Don't add per-agent buffering \"to avoid TUI thrash\" — the viewport handles that\n  - Don't change the AgentReviewer interface — extend parsers in place\n\n  Useful cont