{"parentUuid":"1387995b-1cc4-4ced-b5a2-633d33e53792","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1ec9ed76-4982-4973-85e2-3f6d3abc155e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SYjFa6Wm4RtVMB6rexnMaJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Package types — see reviewer.go for package-level rationale.\n2\t//\n3\t// template.go provides ReviewerTemplate, a struct that implements\n4\t// AgentReviewer using two caller-supplied functions: BuildCmd (per-agent\n5\t// argv/env construction) and Parser (per-agent stdout-to-Event stream).\n6\t//\n7\t// All three currently-supported agents (claude-code, codex, gemini-cli)\n8\t// share the Start/Process/Wait/Events scaffolding. Only the build-cmd\n9\t// step and the stdout parser genuinely differ. The template owns the\n10\t// shared lifecycle (spawn → pipe stdout → run parser → forward events\n11\t// → close on exit); each agent supplies the two unique pieces.\n12\tpackage types\n13\t\n14\timport (\n15\t\t\"context\"\n16\t\t\"errors\"\n17\t\t\"fmt\"\n18\t\t\"io\"\n19\t\t\"os/exec\"\n20\t\t\"strings\"\n21\t)\n22\t\n23\tconst maxProcessStderrBytes = 64 * 1024\n24\t\n25\t// ReviewerTemplate implements AgentReviewer for agents whose only per-agent\n26\t// quirks are argv/env construction and stdout parsing. Both fields must be\n27\t// set before Start is called; nil values cause Start to panic immediately.\n28\ttype ReviewerTemplate struct {\n29\t\t// AgentName is returned by Name(). Stable identifier per agent.\n30\t\tAgentName string\n31\t\n32\t\t// BuildCmd constructs the *exec.Cmd to spawn the agent process,\n33\t\t// including argv, stdin (if any), and ENTIRE_REVIEW_* env vars.\n34\t\t// The command MUST NOT have started yet; the template will call Start.\n35\t\tBuildCmd func(ctx context.Context, cfg RunConfig) *exec.Cmd\n36\t\n37\t\t// Parser converts the agent's stdout stream into a sequence of Events.\n38\t\t// The returned channel must close when stdout closes. Implementations\n39\t\t// must emit Started