{"parentUuid":"2e5a6685-3405-4124-a6b4-4a42f9e7cd8c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1ec9ed76-4982-4973-85e2-3f6d3abc155e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ELPkDcUFcfghkiJatTPTVb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Package review — see env.go for package-level rationale.\n2\t//\n3\t// run_multi.go implements RunMulti, the N-agent orchestrator. It runs each\n4\t// AgentReviewer in its own goroutine under a shared context, fans their\n5\t// event streams into a single dispatch loop that calls each Sink serially\n6\t// (preserving the serial-dispatch contract from CU4), and aggregates the\n7\t// per-agent results into a single RunSummary.\n8\t//\n9\t// Cancellation: when ctx is cancelled (typically by the cobra command's\n10\t// SIGINT handling), all per-agent reviewers see ctx.Err() via their\n11\t// individual Process implementations and exit. RunMulti waits for every\n12\t// goroutine to drain before returning, ensuring no AgentEvent calls fire\n13\t// after RunFinished.\n14\t//\n15\t// Goroutine accounting for N agents:\n16\t//   - N forwarding goroutines: one per agent that started successfully,\n17\t//     reads proc.Events() and sends tagged events to the fan-in channel.\n18\t//   - 1 channel-close goroutine: waits for all N forwarders via WaitGroup\n19\t//     then closes the fan-in channel so the dispatch loop terminates.\n20\t//   - 1 dispatch goroutine (the caller's): ranges over fan-in, updates\n21\t//     per-agent state, calls sinks serially. RunMulti does NOT spawn a\n22\t//     separate dispatch goroutine — the fan-in loop runs on the RunMulti\n23\t//     call stack, keeping the goroutine count low.\n24\tpackage review\n25\t\n26\timport (\n27\t\t\"context\"\n28\t\t\"sync\"\n29\t\t\"time\"\n30\t\n31\t\treviewtypes \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/types\"\n32\t)\n33\t\n34\t// perAgentState tracks the mutable accumulation for one agent during a\n35\t// multi-agent run.\n36\t//\n37\t// Write paths (