{"parentUuid":"5e6316d6-6b08-4b70-a396-29cca67e7f29","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016jQ8P1S35UeLCViiGkC4KC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass and lint is clean. Here's the summary.\n\n★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\nThe brief's diagnosis (\"each adapter waits for the full stdout before parsing\") didn't match what the parsers actually do — all three use `bufio.Scanner`, which is line-by-line. The new `TestParseClaudeOutput_StreamsPerLine` test pins that proof in code. The real cause is a layer below: when stdout is a pipe, libc/Rust/Node's `isatty(stdout)` returns false and the runtime switches to block-buffered output. Allocating a PTY makes `isatty` return true so per-line flushing resumes — and stderr stays on a separate pipe so the existing bounded-stderr diagnostics still work.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n## What changed\n\n**Diagnosis first (test before fix):**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go:239` — `TestParseClaudeOutput_StreamsPerLine` drips lines through `io.Pipe` and asserts events arrive between writes, proving the parser is already line-by-line streaming. This pins the bug *upstream* of our code.\n\n**Instrumentation (gated by debug logging):**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/run_multi.go:158` and `cmd/entire/cli/review/run.go:69` — single `logging.Debug` call in each dispatch loop tagging per-event arrivals with `agent`, `kind`, `since_started`. Off by default; flip `log_level=DEBUG` to capture the same timing trace the brief asked for.\n\n**PTY fix (the actual streaming behaviour):**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go` — added `UsePTY bool` field on `ReviewerTemplate`. When set, `Start()` allocates `pty.Open()`, points `cmd.Stdout` at the slave, keeps `cmd.Stderr` on a separate pipe (so the bounded-stderr diagnostics tested by `TestReviewerTemplate_WaitIncludesStderrOnFailure` still work), and wraps