{"parentUuid":"d8ca7860-c180-4efe-8860-178a554b31be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01ShsjvZvwDVdxQKRfaiaoo7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, that's the cleanest way to confirm the actual user-visible behaviour, since unit tests can't reproduce \"agent buffers when stdout is a pipe\" without spawning real agent processes.\n\n★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\nPTY mode only helps if the agent's *runtime* (libc/Node/Rust) is the layer doing the buffering — that flips off as soon as `isatty(stdout)` returns true. If an agent does its own *application-level* aggregation (e.g., builds the full response in memory and prints once), no PTY trick rescues that — the smoke test is the only way to tell which agents fall in which bucket.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n## Suggested smoke test\n\n1. Make sure you have two launchable agents configured in `.entire/settings.json` under `review` — e.g. `claude-code` and `codex`.\n2. Optionally enable debug logging to get a timestamped trace alongside the visual check:\n   ```\n   echo '{\"log_level\":\"DEBUG\"}' > .entire/settings.local.json\n   ```\n   (or merge that key into an existing file).\n3. Build and run:\n   ```\n   mise run build\n   ./entire review\n   ```\n4. As soon as the dashboard appears, hit **Ctrl+O** to drill into one agent's event buffer. You should see the event count climb while the agent is still working — not jump from 0 to N at end-of-run.\n5. After the run, look at `.entire/logs/*.log` for `review event arrived` entries. The `since_started` field should stagger over the run, not cluster at the end.\n\n## What to look for per agent\n\n- **claude-code** with `-p` text mode: I'd expect this to stream now — Anthropic's CLI flushes per token batch.\n- **codex** (Rust): should also stream now; the Rust stdio LineWriter pairs well with PTY-isatty.\n- **gemini-cli**: Node-based — most exposed to runtime buffering; PTY should help most here.\n\nIf any one of them still bursts at the end, that's an app-level aggregation problem in that specific CLI — different fix (likely an agent-specific flag like `--output-format stream-json` for claude). Tell me which agent shows it and I'll dig into that one.\n\nIf everything streams cleanly, you can revert the `log_level` change and ship."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159775,"cache_read_input_tokens":21018,"output_tokens":769,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":159775,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":769,"cache_read_input_tokens":21018,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159775,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":159775},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CawuJk28BYQj6E1nqgSB5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b50a4a58-9842-4db2-b2a8-a6b455612914","timestamp":"2026-05-12T02:41:26.475Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-progress-stream","sessionId":"29e905db-df81-4eac-9e54-265c4e180a9c","version":"2.1.139","gitBranch":"review-fix-progress-stream"}
