{"parentUuid":"f1c66992-37dd-44e1-8a66-e2ceab6a31ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01YYdEfRhk4Wh2ecEUHQs5jK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right — I had the bug nailed and then talked myself out of it when the `say hi` baseline finished quickly. That was a misread: a 1-word response can't *show* streaming whether or not it's enabled. For a real long review, claude `-p` plain-text mode does indeed dump everything at exit, which is exactly what the brief was complaining about and exactly what Ctrl+O is supposed to fix.\n\nSo the streaming-flag route the brief gestured at (\"claude-code uses stream-json output\") is the actual fix, and I should have gone there first instead of the PTY detour. The fix per agent:\n\n- **claude-code**: `claude -p <prompt> --output-format stream-json --verbose` emits newline-delimited JSON events: `{\"type\":\"system\",...}` once at start, then `{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"...\"}]...}}` as text streams in, then `{\"type\":\"result\",...}` at end. Parser switches from bufio.Scanner-of-text-lines to bufio.Scanner-of-JSON-lines, decoding each line and emitting an `AssistantText` per text delta. Tool-use events become `ToolCall`. Token totals from the `result` event become a final `Tokens` event.\n- **codex**: needs the equivalent flag — codex CLI has been adding more structured output options. I'll check `codex exec --help` to find it. If it doesn't have one, we keep codex on the current parser (it does emit chrome-then-response with newlines, which can stream over a pipe — the original \"burst at end\" might be claude-specific).\n- **gemini-cli**: similar — `gemini -p` may have a JSON streaming mode.\n\nBefore I write code, two things I'd like to confirm with one cheap test you can run yourself:\n\n```\nclaude -p \"write a 200-word essay about cats\" --output-format stream-json --verbose\n```\n\nIf you see JSON lines printing **incrementally** (one every few hundred ms) as the model writes, we've confirmed the streaming flag does what we need. If the JSON also dumps all at once at the end, claude's `-p` mode doesn't stream regardless of format and we have a bigger problem.\n\n```\ncodex exec --help 2>&1 | grep -iE \"json|format|stream\"\n```\n\nThat'll tell us what codex offers.\n\nRun those two and paste the output, and I'll implement the parser changes. To set expectations: this is a bigger change than the (now-cleaned-up) PTY attempt — it touches each agent's parser to handle a new on-the-wire format. But it's the right shape: change is in pipe mode where the agents behave well, change is per-agent (matches the brief's \"extend parsers in place\"), and there's a clean way to test it with captured JSONL fixtures (no API needed for unit tests).\n\nI owe you a more careful read of the brief next time — the \"stream-json output\" line was literally pointing at the answer."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2024,"cache_read_input_tokens":305253,"output_tokens":2504,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2024,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2504,"cache_read_input_tokens":305253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2024},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caxr9Qn9KgAKEiDBWE4RR","type":"assistant","uuid":"4eaa1a90-5dd5-44df-a4d9-74c65570c126","timestamp":"2026-05-12T14:40:47.362Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-progress-stream","sessionId":"29e905db-df81-4eac-9e54-265c4e180a9c","version":"2.1.139","gitBranch":"review-fix-progress-s