{"parentUuid":"dfbe7174-685a-47ba-8f78-66bdad8786a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01PsMerZQsXvwRboAMnzGGJw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That output is the key data point. Look at what claude's stream-json actually emits:\n\n```\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"hook_started\", ...}     ← many of these at start (~1-2s)\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"hook_response\", ...}    ← responses to each hook\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"init\", ...}              ← config event\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",...}]}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"...full essay...\"}]}}\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\", ...}           ← final summary\n```\n\n★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\nWhat you saw appearing \"every couple seconds\" is event-level streaming, not token-level. The system/hook events spread out over the startup phase, then there's a model-thinking pause, then the assistant message arrives as one whole text block (the full essay in a single JSON line), then the result event. For a 200-word essay (one model turn, no tool use), that's the natural shape. For a real PR review the agent will issue multiple Read/Bash tool calls, and each one produces its own assistant + tool_result event — those punctuate the run with visible progress, which is exactly the \"Ctrl+O surfaces progress\" experience the bug was about.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nSo the parser change becomes:\n- Read JSON line-by-line (`bufio.Scanner`, but each `Text()` is a JSON envelope).\n- Dispatch by `type`:\n  - `assistant.content[*]` of type `text` → emit `AssistantText`\n  - `assistant.content[*]` of type `tool_use` → emit `ToolCall{Name: name, Args: JSON(input)}`\n  - `assistant.content[*]` of type `thinking` → skip (or emit redacted)\n  - `result` → emit final `Tokens` from `usage`, then `Finished{Success: !is_error}`\n  - `system` / `user` / `rate_limit_event` → skip\n- Also pass `--verbose` (stream-json requires it).\n\nI'll wait on your codex output before writing code — if codex has the equivalent flag we do both agents at once; if not, only claude needs the swap and codex stays on its current parser (it does interleave exec blocks and chrome between assistant lines, which gives natural per-line cadence over a pipe).\n\nTake your time on the codex test."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17911,"cache_read_input_tokens":307277,"output_tokens":3374,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17911,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3374,"cache_read_input_tokens":307277,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17911},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caxs2JXmsHCcJWYA3L73k","type":"assistant","uuid":"ddd2ed24-68b2-4686-b096-3bb228414ec6","timestamp":"2026-05-12T14:52:31.362Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-progress-stream","sessionId":"29e905db-df81-4eac-9e54-265c4e180a9c","version":"2.1.139","gitBranch":"review-fix-progress-stream"}
