{"parentUuid":"172043fb-9b45-48ae-bdcf-bad2df4e7243","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0152qr3GnE2P7cpSFRaVEYVx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FCcyZ24Mko6AvE4hHhvdGw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-progress-stream/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-review-streaming-json.md","content":"# Review Live-Streaming via Per-Agent JSON Output Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Make `entire review`'s Ctrl+O drill-in show in-progress agent output (tool calls, assistant messages) as the agents work, instead of dumping everything at end of run.\n\n**Architecture:** The current parsers consume plain-text stdout from `claude -p` and `codex exec -`. Both CLIs only emit text to stdout when the model has finished generating, so the drill-in buffer stays at `[started]` for the whole run and the dashboard preview only populates at end. The fix is to switch each agent to its own JSONL streaming mode (`claude … --output-format stream-json --verbose` and `codex exec … --json`), which emits one JSON envelope per agent-side event (`assistant.message` for claude; `item.started`/`item.completed`/`turn.completed` for codex). The parsers become line-delimited JSON decoders, each dispatching by `type` and emitting our existing `Event` variants (`AssistantText`, `ToolCall`, `Tokens`, `Finished`). No PTY, no change to the AgentReviewer / Process / Sink interfaces.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26 · github.com/spf13/cobra · charm.land/bubbletea/v2 (TUI sink) · `encoding/json` · `bufio.Scanner` (NDJSON line splitter) · existing `cmd/entire/cli/agent/{claudecode,codex,geminicli}` packages · `cmd/entire/cli/review/types` template.\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n### Why the current plain-text parsers fail\n\n`claude -p <prompt>` in default text mode and `codex exec --skip-git-repo-check -` both buffer their output until the model finishes generating. The empirical evidence (from the user's manual A/B test on 2026-05-12):\n\n- `claude -p \"say hi\"` → 10s wall, output dumps at end.\n- `codex exec -` → 20s wall, full chrome + response at end.\n- During a real review the drill-in stays at `[started]` for both agents until the very last second, when N events arrive in a burst. This is the user-visible bug the brief described as \"events arrive batched at end of run\".\n\nA previous attempt to fix this with PTY mode (route stdout through `pty.Open()` so isatty returns true) was reverted: the real agents change output shape under a TTY (cursor-rewriting / no newlines), so the parser saw zero `AssistantText` events. That history is in commits on `review-fix-progress-stream` worktree and should not be repeated.\n\n### Why JSONL mode does fix it\n\nBoth CLIs emit ONE JSON envelope per logical agent event, with a newline between envelopes. When the agent issues a tool call we get `item.started` (codex) / `assistant tool_use` (claude) immediately, BEFORE the tool runs. When the agent emits a chunk of text we get one envelope per message. For a real review (lots of `Read`/`Bash`/`Grep` tool use, interleaved analysis text) this gives ~10-50 events per agent run, spread over the full duration.\n\n### What the live JSON looks like\n\nCaptured manually on 2026-05-12 from the worktree shell. Stored as fixtures in the test directories.\n\n**claude `--output-format stream-json --verbose`:**\n\n```\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"hook_started\", …}        ← multiple, ignore\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"hook_response\", …}       ← multiple, ignore\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"init\", …}                ← one, ignore\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"…\"}], …}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"…assistant prose…\"}], …}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"…\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{…}}], …}}   ← only on tool-use turns\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\", …}]}}                                       ← echoes, ignore\n{\"type\":\"rate_limit_event\", …}                       ← ignore\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"duration_ms\":…,\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"…\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":…,\"output_tokens\":…,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":…,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":…}}\n```\n\n**codex `exec --json`:**\n\n```\n{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"…\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"…\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"…\",\"aggregated_output\":\"…\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"…assistant text…\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":…,\"cached_input_tokens\":…,\"output_tokens\":…,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":…}}\n```\n\nCodex's live JSON shape is **different** from the persisted-transcript shape in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/transcript.go` — do not reuse that schema. The live shape is documented above; the parser must match it exactly.\n\n### Anti-features (do not introduce)\n\n- **No PTY.** Pipe-mode JSONL is sufficient. The previous PTY attempt broke the agents.\n- **No backwards-compat for the old plain-text parser.** Once we switch argv, the old format is unreachable. Delete the old parser code paths, not behind a feature flag.\n- **No new agent in this PR.** gemini-cli stays on its current parser; if streaming is wanted there it's a follow-up.\n- **No throttling / coalescing of events in the TUI.** Per-event dispatch is intentional. PR #1184 already fixed the drill-in viewport for this.\n- **Codex chrome filter (`output_filter.go`) is dead code under `--json`.** Remove it once tests no longer reference it. (Confirm with `grep -rn \"FilterLine\\|codex.Strip\" cmd/` before deleting.)\n\n### Related skills\n\n- @superpowers:test-driven-development — write each parser test first, run, watch fail, then implement.\n- @superpowers:systematic-debugging — only re-enter if a test fails for a non-obvious reason. Don't preemptively chase ghosts.\n- @superpowers:verification-before-completion — run `mise run check` before declaring the work done.\n\n---\n\n## File Structure\n\n### Files to modify (existing)\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go` — change `BuildCmd` argv (add `--output-format stream-json --verbose`); rewrite `parseClaudeOutput` to decode NDJSON; keep `NewReviewer` shape.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go` — update `TestReviewer_ArgvShape`; replace `TestReviewer_EventStream` to read a JSONL fixture; drop `TestParseClaudeOutput_StreamsPerLine` (it pinned the *line-by-line text* contract, which no longer applies; the new fixture test is the replacement).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/canned_session.txt` — delete.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer.go` — change `BuildCmd` argv (add `--json`); rewrite `parseCodexOutput` to decode NDJSON.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer_test.go` — update argv test; replace event-stream test with JSONL fixture test.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/output_filter.go` — DELETE the file once nothing references `FilterLine` / `Strip` / `collectFinalCodexLine`. Confirm first.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/output_filter_test.go` — DELETE alongside.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer.go` — drop the now-unused `csiRegex` / `execBlockRegex` / `bannerRegex` / `hookFiringRegex` / `timestampLogRegex` / `isCodexMetadataLine` / role-marker helpers that the old text parser used. If any are referenced from another codex file, leave them; do not blindly delete.\n- `CLAUDE.md` — `entire review` section already mentions argv shapes for each agent; update the two sentences that quote the old argv to quote the new argv. No structural change.\n\n### Files to create\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_session.jsonl` — the user's captured 200-word essay run, lightly trimmed to ~10 lines (drop redundant hook events, keep one of each shape).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/json_session.jsonl` — the user's captured \"say hi\" --json run, verbatim (6 lines).\n\n### Files NOT to touch\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go` — already correct, no UsePTY field.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/run.go` / `run_multi.go` — already correct, no debug instrumentation.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_sink.go` / `tui_model.go` / `tui_detail.go` — viewport handling is correct per PR #1184.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/reviewer.go` — out of scope; gemini stays on plain text.\n- `e2e/streaming-smoke/` — does not exist (cleanup removed it earlier).\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: claude-code stream-json parser\n\n### Task 1: Capture the JSONL fixture\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_session.jsonl`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Save a minimal fixture**\n\nCopy the user's captured stream from the 2026-05-12 session into the file. Keep at minimum: one `system/init`, one `assistant` with a `thinking` content block (empty thinking, signature scrubbed to `\"REDACTED\"` so the fixture stays small), one `assistant` with a `text` content block, one `result` event with `is_error: false` and `usage`. Drop the dozen `hook_started` / `hook_response` events — they're all the same shape, one is enough to pin the \"ignore system events\" branch.\n\nThe fixture should be 6-10 lines total and end with the `result` line.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Verify the fixture is valid NDJSON**\n\nRun: `while IFS= read -r line; do echo \"$line\" | jq -e . >/dev/null || echo BAD; done < cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_session.jsonl`\nExpected: no `BAD` lines printed.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Commit the fixture**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_session.jsonl\ngit commit -m \"test(review): capture claude stream-json fixture\"\n```\n\n### Task 2: Write the failing fixture test\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace `TestReviewer_EventStream` with a fixture test that decodes JSONL**\n\nRead the existing test for structure. The new test reads `testdata/stream_session.jsonl`, feeds it to `parseClaudeOutput`, drains the channel, and asserts:\n\n```go\nfunc TestParseClaudeOutput_DecodesStreamJSON(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    data, err := os.ReadFile(\"testdata/stream_session.jsonl\")\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"read fixture: %v\", err)\n    }\n    events := collectEvents(parseClaudeOutput(strings.NewReader(string(data))))\n\n    // First event always Started.\n    if _, ok := events[0].(reviewtypes.Started); !ok {\n        t.Errorf(\"events[0] = %T, want Started\", events[0])\n    }\n    // Last event always Finished{Success: true}.\n    last := events[len(events)-1]\n    fin, ok := last.(reviewtypes.Finished)\n    if !ok || !fin.Success {\n        t.Errorf(\"last event = %v, want Finished{Success:true}\", last)\n    }\n\n    // Must see at least one AssistantText with the fixture's prose.\n    var sawText bool\n    for _, ev := range events {\n        if at, ok := ev.(reviewtypes.AssistantText); ok && strings.Contains(at.Text, \"EXPECTED-WORD\") {\n            sawText = true\n        }\n    }\n    if !sawText {\n        t.Error(\"expected AssistantText carrying fixture prose\")\n    }\n\n    // Must see exactly one Tokens event with non-zero output_tokens.\n    var tokensSeen int\n    var tokensOut int\n    for _, ev := range events {\n        if tk, ok := ev.(reviewtypes.Tokens); ok {\n            tokensSeen++\n            tokensOut = tk.Out\n        }\n    }\n    if tokensSeen != 1 {\n        t.Errorf(\"Tokens count = %d, want 1\", tokensSeen)\n    }\n    if tokensOut == 0 {\n        t.Error(\"Tokens.Out = 0, want > 0\")\n    }\n}\n```\n\nReplace `EXPECTED-WORD` with a literal that's actually in your captured fixture (e.g. `\"Cats are\"` for the essay sample).\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Drop the obsolete `TestParseClaudeOutput_StreamsPerLine` test**\n\nIt pinned the line-by-line *text* contract. The new parser is line-by-line *JSON*; the contract is now tested by the fixture test plus `TestParseClaudeOutput_ReportsScannerError` (which can stay — bufio.Scanner errors still apply to NDJSON).\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run the new test — it must fail**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/ -run TestParseClaudeOutput_DecodesStreamJSON -v -count=1`\nExpected: FAIL (current parser emits one `AssistantText` per RAW JSON line; no `Tokens` event emitted at all).\n\n### Task 3: Rewrite parseClaudeOutput\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace the parser body**\n\nThe new parser reads NDJSON. Each line is one event envelope. Dispatch by `type` field. Skip `system`, `user`, `rate_limit_event`. For `assistant`, iterate `message.content[]`:\n\n```go\npackage claudecode\n\nimport (\n    \"bufio\"\n    \"context\"\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"os/exec\"\n\n    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review\"\n    reviewtypes \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/types\"\n)\n\n// parseClaudeOutput converts claude's --output-format stream-json --verbose\n// stdout into a stream of Events. Each stdout line is one JSON envelope:\n//   - {\"type\":\"system\",...}      session metadata, hooks; swallowed\n//   - {\"type\":\"assistant\",...}   one content block at a time; text → AssistantText,\n//                                tool_use → ToolCall, thinking → swallowed\n//   - {\"type\":\"user\",...}        tool_result echoes; swallowed\n//   - {\"type\":\"result\",...}      final summary; emits Tokens then Finished\n//\n// Emits Started first, Finished{Success:...} last (success follows result.is_error).\n// On a scanner error (torn stream), emits RunError then Finished{Success:false}.\n//\n// Exposed for golden-file contract testing.\nfunc parseClaudeOutput(r io.Reader) <-chan reviewtypes.Event {\n    out := make(chan reviewtypes.Event, 32)\n    go func() {\n        defer close(out)\n        out <- reviewtypes.Started{}\n        scanner := bufio.NewScanner(r)\n        // Stream-json messages can carry full tool-input payloads; size headroom.\n        scanner.Buffer(make([]byte, 1024*1024), 16*1024*1024)\n        var finalResult *claudeResultEnvelope\n        for scanner.Scan() {\n            line := scanner.Bytes()\n            if len(line) == 0 {\n                continue\n            }\n            var env claudeEnvelope\n            if err := json.Unmarshal(line, &env); err != nil {\n                // Garbled line: surface as RunError but keep parsing — one bad\n                // line should not tear the whole stream.\n                out <- reviewtypes.RunError{Err: fmt.Errorf(\"claude stream-json: %w\", err)}\n                continue\n            }\n            switch env.Type {\n            case \"assistant\":\n                for _, block := range env.Message.Content {\n                    switch block.Type {\n                    case \"text\":\n                        if block.Text != \"\" {\n                            out <- reviewtypes.AssistantText{Text: block.Text}\n                        }\n                    case \"tool_use\":\n                        args, _ := json.Marshal(block.Input) //nolint:errcheck\n                        out <- reviewtypes.ToolCall{Name: block.Name, Args: string(args)}\n                    // \"thinking\" intentionally swallowed.\n                    }\n                }\n            case \"result\":\n                cp := env\n                finalResult = &claudeResultEnvelope{\n                    IsError: env.IsError,\n                    Usage:   env.Usage,\n                }\n                _ = cp\n            // \"system\", \"user\", \"rate_limit_event\" swallowed.\n            }\n        }\n        if err := scanner.Err(); err != nil {\n            out <- reviewtypes.RunError{Err: fmt.Errorf(\"read stdout: %w\", err)}\n            out <- reviewtypes.Finished{Success: false}\n            return\n        }\n        if finalResult != nil {\n            in := finalResult.Usage.InputTokens + finalResult.Usage.CacheReadInputTokens + finalResult.Usage.CacheCreationInputTokens\n            out <- reviewtypes.Tokens{In: in, Out: finalResult.Usage.OutputTokens}\n            out <- reviewtypes.Finished{Success: !finalResult.IsError}\n            return\n        }\n        // No result envelope arrived — treat as torn stream.\n        out <- reviewtypes.Finished{Success: false}\n    }()\n    return out\n}\n\n// Envelope types. Fields kept minimal — anything we don't need stays\n// untyped (omitted from the struct) and the json decoder ignores it.\ntype claudeEnvelope struct {\n    Type    string          `json:\"type\"`\n    Message claudeMessage   `json:\"message\"`\n    IsError bool            `json:\"is_error\"`\n    Usage   claudeUsage     `json:\"usage\"`\n}\n\ntype claudeMessage struct {\n    Content []claudeBlock `json:\"content\"`\n}\n\ntype claudeBlock struct {\n    Type  string          `json:\"type\"`\n    Text  string          `json:\"text\"`\n    Name  string          `json:\"name\"`\n    Input json.RawMessage `json:\"input\"`\n}\n\ntype claudeUsage struct {\n    InputTokens              int `json:\"input_tokens\"`\n    OutputTokens             int `json:\"output_tokens\"`\n    CacheReadInputTokens     int `json:\"cache_read_input_tokens\"`\n    CacheCreationInputTokens int `json:\"cache_creation_input_tokens\"`\n}\n\ntype claudeResultEnvelope struct {\n    IsError bool\n    Usage   claudeUsage\n}\n```\n\nDrop the unused `cp` / `_ = cp` lines and the `claudeResultEnvelope` indirection if simpler — the goal is one structurally-typed decode per line.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Update buildReviewCmd argv**\n\n```go\nfunc buildReviewCmd(ctx context.Context, cfg reviewtypes.RunConfig) *exec.Cmd {\n    prompt := review.ComposeReviewPrompt(cfg)\n    cmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, \"claude\", \"-p\", prompt, \"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"--verbose\")\n    cmd.Env = review.AppendReviewEnv(os.Environ(), \"claude-code\", cfg, prompt)\n    return cmd\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Update the package doc comment on `NewReviewer`**\n\nOld comment says \"Plain-text stdout … no JSON envelope\". Replace with: argv shape and that stdout is newline-delimited JSON envelopes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run the fixture test — must pass**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/ -run TestParseClaudeOutput_DecodesStreamJSON -v -count=1`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Run the package's full test suite**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/ -count=1`\nExpected: PASS. `TestReviewer_ArgvShape` will fail because it still expects the old argv — that's the next task.\n\n### Task 4: Update argv shape test for claude\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Update `TestReviewer_ArgvShape` to expect new argv**\n\n```go\nfunc TestReviewer_ArgvShape(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    cfg := reviewtypes.RunConfig{Skills: []string{\"/skill-a\"}, PerRunPrompt: \"extra context\"}\n    cmd := buildReviewCmd(context.Background(), cfg)\n\n    want := []string{\"claude\", \"-p\", \"\", \"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"--verbose\"}\n    if len(cmd.Args) != len(want) {\n        t.Fatalf(\"argv length = %d, want %d: %v\", len(cmd.Args), len(want), cmd.Args)\n    }\n    for i, w := range want {\n        if i == 2 {\n            // prompt — must be non-empty but content is not pinned here.\n            if cmd.Args[2] == \"\" {\n                t.Error(\"Args[2] (prompt) is empty\")\n            }\n            continue\n        }\n        if cmd.Args[i] != w {\n            t.Errorf(\"Args[%d] = %q, want %q\", i, cmd.Args[i], w)\n        }\n    }\n    for _, arg := range cmd.Args {\n        if arg == \"--continue\" || arg == \"-c\" || arg == \"--resume\" || arg == \"-r\" {\n            t.Fatalf(\"Args must start a fresh Claude review, got resume/continue flag in %v\", cmd.Args)\n        }\n    }\n    if cmd.Stdin != nil {\n        t.Errorf(\"cmd.Stdin = %v, want nil (claude uses argv, not stdin)\", cmd.Stdin)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Delete `testdata/canned_session.txt`**\n\n```bash\nrm cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/canned_session.txt\n```\n\nThe old plain-text fixture is no longer referenced. Verify with: `grep -rn \"canned_session\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/` → no hits.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run package tests**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/ -count=1`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Commit chunk 1**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/\ngit commit -m \"feat(review): stream claude-code via --output-format stream-json\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 2: codex --json parser\n\n### Task 5: Capture the codex JSONL fixture\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/json_session.jsonl`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Save the captured fixture verbatim**\n\nSave the six lines from the user's \"say hi in one word\" run (2026-05-12) to `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/json_session.jsonl`. Keep the long `aggregated_output` (the embedded SKILL.md dump) — it stress-tests the scanner buffer size. Strip the personal session id by replacing it with `\"019e1cad-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\"` for deterministic tests.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Verify NDJSON**\n\nRun: `while IFS= read -r line; do echo \"$line\" | jq -e . >/dev/null || echo BAD; done < cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/json_session.jsonl`\nExpected: no `BAD` lines.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/json_session.jsonl\ngit commit -m \"test(review): capture codex --json fixture\"\n```\n\n### Task 6: Write the failing codex fixture test\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Add `TestParseCodexOutput_DecodesJSONStream`**\n\n```go\nfunc TestParseCodexOutput_DecodesJSONStream(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    data, err := os.ReadFile(\"testdata/json_session.jsonl\")\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"read fixture: %v\", err)\n    }\n    events := collectCodexEvents(parseCodexOutput(strings.NewReader(string(data))))\n\n    // First Started.\n    if _, ok := events[0].(reviewtypes.Started); !ok {\n        t.Errorf(\"events[0] = %T, want Started\", events[0])\n    }\n    // Last Finished{Success:true}.\n    last := events[len(events)-1]\n    fin, ok := last.(reviewtypes.Finished)\n    if !ok || !fin.Success {\n        t.Errorf(\"last event = %v, want Finished{Success:true}\", last)\n    }\n    // Expect at least one ToolCall (command_execution) and one AssistantText (agent_message).\n    var sawTool, sawText bool\n    for _, ev := range events {\n        if tc, ok := ev.(reviewtypes.ToolCall); ok && tc.Name == \"exec\" {\n            sawTool = true\n        }\n        if at, ok := ev.(reviewtypes.AssistantText); ok && at.Text == \"Hi\" {\n            sawText = true\n        }\n    }\n    if !sawTool {\n        t.Error(\"expected ToolCall{Name: exec} from item.started/command_execution\")\n    }\n    if !sawText {\n        t.Error(\"expected AssistantText{Text: Hi} from item.completed/agent_message\")\n    }\n    // Tokens event present with non-zero output.\n    var tokensSeen int\n    for _, ev := range events {\n        if tk, ok := ev.(reviewtypes.Tokens); ok && tk.Out > 0 {\n            tokensSeen++\n        }\n    }\n    if tokensSeen != 1 {\n        t.Errorf(\"Tokens with Out>0 count = %d, want 1\", tokensSeen)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc collectCodexEvents(ch <-chan reviewtypes.Event) []reviewtypes.Event {\n    var events []reviewtypes.Event\n    for ev := range ch {\n        events = append(events, ev)\n    }\n    return events\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run — must fail**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/ -run TestParseCodexOutput_DecodesJSONStream -v -count=1`\nExpected: FAIL. Current parser uses the chrome-line state machine, which decodes none of the JSON envelopes correctly.\n\n### Task 7: Rewrite parseCodexOutput\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace parser body with JSONL decoder**\n\n```go\npackage codex\n\nimport (\n    \"bufio\"\n    \"context\"\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"os/exec\"\n    \"strings\"\n\n    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review\"\n    reviewtypes \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/types\"\n)\n\n// parseCodexOutput converts codex's `exec --json` stdout into a stream of\n// Events. Each stdout line is one JSON envelope (top-level \"type\" field).\n//\n// Envelope types observed in codex 0.130.0:\n//   - thread.started        session id; swallowed\n//   - turn.started          marker; swallowed\n//   - item.started          tool invocation begins → emits ToolCall when\n//                           item.type == \"command_execution\"\n//   - item.completed        tool invocation ends OR an agent_message;\n//                           agent_message → AssistantText\n//   - turn.completed        terminal usage block → Tokens, then Finished\n//\n// On a scanner error or a missing turn.completed envelope, emits RunError\n// then Finished{Success: false}.\n//\n// Exposed for golden-file contract testing.\nfunc parseCodexOutput(r io.Reader) <-chan reviewtypes.Event {\n    out := make(chan reviewtypes.Event