{"parentUuid":"2c4a37f5-cf5b-410e-acf3-cc168a2d9cdd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3c3d7b47-408a-45e9-bdae-abc0991d1ea9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FCcyZ24Mko6AvE4hHhvdGw","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-progress-stream/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-review-streaming-json.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"df1b6dad-9953-4578-a7e1-59b5abf3b0c6","timestamp":"2026-05-12T15:09:58.798Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-progress-stream/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-review-streaming-json.md","content":"# Review Live-Streaming via Per-Agent JSON Output Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Make `entire review`'s Ctrl+O drill-in show in-progress agent output (tool calls, assistant messages) as the agents work, instead of dumping everything at end of run.\n\n**Architecture:** The current parsers consume plain-text stdout from `claude -p` and `codex exec -`. Both CLIs only emit text to stdout when the model has finished generating, so the drill-in buffer stays at `[started]` for the whole run and the dashboard preview only populates at end. The fix is to switch each agent to its own JSONL streaming mode (`claude … --output-format stream-json --verbose` and `codex exec … --json`), which emits one JSON envelope per agent-side event (`assistant.message` for claude; `item.started`/`item.completed`/`turn.completed` for codex). The parsers become line-delimited JSON decoders, each dispatching by `type` and emitting our existing `Event` variants (`AssistantText`, `ToolCall`, `Tokens`, `Finished`). No PTY, no change to the AgentReviewer / Process / Sink interfaces.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26 · github.com/spf13/cobra · charm.land/bubbletea/v2 (TUI sink) · `encoding/json` · `bufio.Scanner` (NDJSON line splitter) · existing `cmd/entire/cli/agent/{claudecode,codex,geminicli}` packages · `cmd/entire/cli/review/types` template.\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n### Why the current plain-text parsers fail\n\n`claude -p <prompt>` in default text mode and `codex exec --skip-git-repo-check -` both buffer their output until the model finishes generating. The empirical evidence (from the user's manual A/B test on 2026-05-12):\n\n- `claude -p \"say hi\"` → 10s wall, output dumps at end.\n- `codex exec -` → 20s wall, full chrome + response at end.\n- During a real review the drill-in stays at `[started]` for both agents until the very last second, when N events arrive in a burst. This is the user-visible bug the brief described as \"events arrive batched at end of run\".\n\nA previous attempt to fix this with PTY mode (route stdout through `pty.Open()` so isatty returns true) was reverted: the real agents change output shape under a TTY (cursor-rewriting / no newlines), so the parser saw zero `AssistantText` events. That history is in commits on `review-fix-progress-stream` worktree and should not be repeated.\n\n### Why JSONL mode does fix it\n\nBoth CLIs emit ONE JSON envelope per logical agent event, with a newline between envelopes. When the agent issues a tool call we get `item.started` (codex) / `assistant tool_use` (claude) immediately, BEFORE the tool runs. When the agent emits a chunk of text we get one envelope per message. For a real review (lots of `Read`/`Bash`/`Grep` tool use, interleaved analysis text) this gives ~10-50 events per agent run, spread over the full duration.\n\n### What the live JSON looks like\n\nCaptured manually on 2026-05-12 from the worktree shell. Stored as fixtures in the test directories.\n\n**claude `--output-format stream-json --verbose`:**\n\n```\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"hook_started\", …}        ← multiple, ignore\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"hook_response\", …}       ← multiple, ignore\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"init\", …}                ← one, ignore\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"…\"}], …}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"…assistant prose…\"}], …}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"…\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{…}}], …}}   ← only on tool-use turns\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\", …}]}}                                       ← echoes, ignore\n{\"type\":\"rate_limit_event\", …}                       ← ignore\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"duration_ms\":…,\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"…\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":…,\"output_tokens\":…,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":…,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":…}}\n```\n\n**codex `exec --json`:**\n\n```\n{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"…\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"…\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"…\",\"aggregated_output\":\"…\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"…assistant text…\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":…,\"cached_input_tokens\":…,\"output_tokens\":…,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":…}}\n```\n\nCodex's live JSON shape is **different** from the persisted-transcript shape in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/transcript.go` — do not reuse that schema. The live shape is documented above; the parser must match it exactly.\n\n### Anti-features (do not introduce)\n\n- **No PTY.** Pipe-mode JSONL is sufficient. The previous PTY attempt broke the agents.\n- **No backwards-compat for the old plain-text parser.** Once we switch argv, the old format is unreachable. Delete the old parser code paths, not behind a feature flag.\n- **No new agent in this PR.** gemini-cli stays on its current parser; if streaming is wanted there it's a follow-up.\n- **No throttling / coalescing of events in the TUI.** Per-event dispatch is intentional. PR #1184 already fixed the drill-in viewport for this.\n- **Codex chrome filter (`output_filter.go`) is dead code under `--json`.** Remove it once tests no longer reference it. (Confirm with `grep -rn \"FilterLine\\|codex.Strip\" cmd/` before deleting.)\n\n### Related skills\n\n- @superpowers:test-driven-development — write each parser test first, run, watch fail, then implement.\n- @superpowers:systematic-debugging — only re-enter if a test fails for a non-obvious reason. Don't preemptively chase ghosts.\n- @superpowers:verification-before-completion — run `mise run check` before declaring the work done.\n\n---\n\n## File Structure\n\n### Files to modify (existing)\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go` — change `BuildCmd` argv (add `--output-format stream-json --verbose`); rewrite `parseClaudeOutput` to decode NDJSON; keep `NewReviewer` shape.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go` — update `TestReviewer_ArgvShape`; replace `TestReviewer_EventStream` to read a JSONL fixture; drop `TestParseClaudeOutput_StreamsPerLine` (it pinned the *line-by-line text* contract, which no longer applies; the new fixture test is the replacement).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/canned_session.txt` — delete.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer.go` — change `BuildCmd` argv (add `--json`); rewrite `parseCodexOutput` to decode NDJSON.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/reviewer_test.go` — update argv test; replace event-stream test with JSONL fixture test.\n- `cmd/entire/cli