small), one `assistant` with a `text` content block, one `result` event with `is_error: false` and `usage`. Drop the dozen `hook_started` / `hook_response` events — they're all the same shape, one is enough to pin the \"ignore system events\" branch.\n\nThe fixture should be 6-10 lines total and end with the `result` line.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Verify the fixture is valid NDJSON**\n\nRun: `while IFS= read -r line; do echo \"$line\" | jq -e . >/dev/null || echo BAD; done < cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_session.jsonl`\nExpected: no `BAD` lines printed.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Commit the fixture**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_session.jsonl\ngit commit -m \"test(review): capture claude stream-json fixture\"\n```\n\n### Task 2: Write the failing fixture test\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace `TestReviewer_EventStream` with a fixture test that decodes JSONL**\n\nRead the existing test for structure. The new test reads `testdata/stream_session.jsonl`, feeds it to `parseClaudeOutput`, drains the channel, and asserts:\n\n```go\nfunc TestParseClaudeOutput_DecodesStreamJSON(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    data, err := os.ReadFile(\"testdata/stream_session.jsonl\")\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"read fixture: %v\", err)\n    }\n    events := collectEvents(parseClaudeOutput(strings.NewReader(string(data))))\n\n    // First event always Started.\n    if _, ok := events[0].(reviewtypes.Started); !ok {\n        t.Errorf(\"events[0] = %T, want Started\", events[0])\n    }\n    // Last event always Finished{Success: true}.\n    last := events[len(events)-1]\n    fin, ok := last.(reviewtypes.Finished)\n    if !ok || !fin.Success {\n        t.Errorf(\"last event = %v, want Finished{Success:true}\", last)\n    }\n\n    // Must see at least one AssistantText with the fixture's prose.\n    var sawText bool\n    for _, ev := range events {\n        if at, ok := ev.(reviewtypes.AssistantText); ok && strings.Contains(at.Text, \"EXPECTED-WORD\") {\n            sawText = true\n        }\n    }\n    if !sawText {\n        t.Error(\"expected AssistantText carrying fixture prose\")\n    }\n\n    // Must see exactly one Tokens event with non-zero output_tokens.\n    var tokensSeen int\n    var tokensOut int\n    for _, ev := range events {\n        if tk, ok := ev.(reviewtypes.Tokens); ok {\n            tokensSeen++\n            tokensOut = tk.Out\n        }\n    }\n    if tokensSeen != 1 {\n        t.Errorf(\"Tokens count = %d, want 1\", tokensSeen)\n    }\n    if tokensOut == 0 {\n        t.Error(\"Tokens.Out = 0, want > 0\")\n    }\n}\n```\n\nReplace `EXPECTED-WORD` with a literal that's actually in your captured fixture (e.g. `\"Cats are\"` for the essay sample).\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Drop the obsolete `TestParseClaudeOutput_StreamsPerLine` test**\n\nIt pinned the line-by-line *text* contract. The new parser is line-by-line *JSON*; the contract is now tested by the fixture test plus `TestParseClaudeOutput_ReportsScannerError` (which can stay — bufio.Scanner errors still apply to NDJSON).\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run the new test — it must fail**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/ -run TestParseClaudeOutput_DecodesStreamJSON -v -count=1`\nExpected: FAIL (current parser emits one `AssistantText` per RAW JSON line; no `Tokens` event emitted at all).\n\n### Task 3: Rewrite parseClaudeOutput\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace the parser body**\n\nThe new parser reads NDJSON. Each line is one event envelope. Dispatch by `type` field. Skip `system`, `user`, `rate_limit_event`. For `assistant`, iterate `message.content[]`:\n\n```go\npackage claudecode\n\nimport (\n    \"bufio\"\n    \"context\"\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"os/exec\"\n\n    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review\"\n    reviewtypes \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/types\"\n)\n\n// parseClaudeOutput converts claude's --output-format stream-json --verbose\n// stdout into a stream of Events. Each stdout line is one JSON envelope:\n//   - {\"type\":\"system\",...}      session metadata, hooks; swallowed\n//   - {\"type\":\"assistant\",...}   one content block at a time; text → AssistantText,\n//                                tool_use → ToolCall, thinking → swallowed\n//   - {\"type\":\"user\",...}        tool_result echoes; swallowed\n//   - {\"type\":\"result\",...}      final summary; emits Tokens then Finished\n//\n// Emits Started first, Finished{Success:...} last (success follows result.is_error).\n// On a scanner error (torn stream), emits RunError then Finished{Success:false}.\n//\n// Exposed for golden-file contract testing.\nfunc parseClaudeOutput(r io.Reader) <-chan reviewtypes.Event {\n    out := make(chan reviewtypes.Event, 32)\n    go func() {\n        defer close(out)\n        out <- reviewtypes.Started{}\n        scanner := bufio.NewScanner(r)\n        // Stream-json messages can carry full tool-input payloads; size headroom.\n        scanner.Buffer(make([]byte, 1024*1024), 16*1024*1024)\n        var finalResult *claudeResultEnvelope\n        for scanner.Scan() {\n            line := scanner.Bytes()\n            if len(line) == 0 {\n                continue\n            }\n            var env claudeEnvelope\n            if err := json.Unmarshal(line, &env); err != nil {\n                // Garbled line: surface as RunError but keep parsing — one bad\n                // line should not tear the whole stream.\n                out <- reviewtypes.RunError{Err: fmt.Errorf(\"claude stream-json: %w\", err)}\n                continue\n            }\n            switch env.Type {\n            case \"assistant\":\n                for _, block := range env.Message.Content {\n                    switch block.Type {\n                    case \"text\":\n                        if block.Text != \"\" {\n                            out <- reviewtypes.AssistantText{Text: block.Text}\n                        }\n                    case \"tool_use\":\n                        args, _ := json.Marshal(block.Input) //nolint:errcheck\n                        out <- reviewtypes.ToolCall{Name: block.Name, Args: string(args)}\n                    // \"thinking\" intentionally swallowed.\n                    }\n                }\n            case \"result\":\n                cp := env\n                finalResult = &claudeResultEnvelope{\n                    IsError: env.IsError,\n                    Usage:   env.Usage,\n                }\n                _ = cp\n            // \"system\", \"user\", \"rate_limit_event\" swallowed.\n            }\n        }\n        if err := scanner.Err(); err != nil {\n            out <- reviewtypes.RunError{Err: fmt.Errorf(\"read stdout: %w\", err)}\n            out <- reviewtypes.Finished{Success: false}\n            return\n        }\n        if finalResult != nil {\n            in := finalResult.Usage.InputTokens + finalResult.Usage.CacheReadInputTokens + finalResult.Usage.CacheCreationInputTokens\n            out <- reviewtypes.Tokens{In: in, Out: finalResult.Usage.OutputTokens}\n            out <- reviewtypes.Finished{Success: !finalResult.IsError}\n            return\n        }\n        // No result envelope arrived — treat as torn stream.\n        out <- reviewtypes.Finished{Success: false}\n    }()\n    return out\n}\n\n// Envelope types. Fields kept minimal — anything we don't need stays\n// untyped (omitted from the struct) and the json decoder ignores it.\ntype claudeEnvelope struct {\n    Type    string          `json:\"type\"`\n    Message claudeMessage   `json:\"message\"`\n    IsError bool            `json:\"is_error\"`\n    Usage   claudeUsage     `json:\"usage\"`\n}\n\ntype claudeMessage struct {\n    Content []claudeBlock `json:\"content\"`\n}\n\ntype claudeBlock struct {\n    Type  string          `json:\"type\"`\n    Text  string          `json:\"text\"`\n    Name  string          `json:\"name\"`\n    Input json.RawMessage `json:\"input\"`\n}\n\ntype claudeUsage struct {\n    InputTokens              int `json:\"input_tokens\"`\n    OutputTokens             int `json:\"output_tokens\"`\n    CacheReadInputTokens     int `json:\"cache_read_input_tokens\"`\n    CacheCreationInputTokens int `json:\"cache_creation_input_tokens\"`\n}\n\ntype claudeResultEnvelope struct {\n    IsError bool\n    Usage   claudeUsage\n}\n```\n\nDrop the unused `cp` / `_ = cp` lines and the `claudeResultEnvelope` indirection if simpler — the goal is one structurally-typed decode per line.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Update buildReviewCmd argv**\n\n```go\nfunc buildReviewCmd(ctx context.Context, cfg reviewtypes.RunConfig) *exec.Cmd {\n    prompt := review.ComposeReviewPrompt(cfg)\n    cmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, \"claude\", \"-p\", prompt, \"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"--verbose\")\n    cmd.Env = review.AppendReviewEnv(os.Environ(), \"claude-code\", cfg, prompt)\n    return cmd\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Update the package doc comment on `NewReviewer`**\n\nOld comment says \"Plain-text stdout … no JSON envelope\". Replace with: argv shape and that stdout is newline-delimited JSON envelopes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run the fixture test — must pass**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/ -run TestParseClaudeOutput_DecodesStreamJSON -v -count=1`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Run the package's full test suite**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/ -count=1`\nExpected: PASS. `TestReviewer_ArgvShape` will fail because it still expects the old argv — that's the next task.\n\n### Task 4: Update argv shape test for claude\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Update `TestReviewer_ArgvShape` to expect new argv**\n\n```go\nfunc TestReviewer_ArgvShape(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    cfg := reviewtypes.RunConfig{Skills: []