{"parentUuid":"4538f908-ff28-4c06-bb10-33fa5217a9ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NCL6mWgqjkvCgBv8HxZUDr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EZCUekWjur94wF9UHozHri","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement chunk 1: claude stream-json","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are implementing Chunk 1 of an `entire review` live-streaming fix.\n\nWorking directory: `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-progress-stream`\nBranch: `review-fix-progress-stream` (confirm with `git branch --show-current` before any edit; if not on this branch, STOP and report BLOCKED).\nBase commit: `40d00ad55`\n\n## Context\n\n`entire review` runs review agents (claude-code, codex, gemini-cli) under a TUI. The bug: drill-in (Ctrl+O) stays at `[started]` because `claude -p <prompt>` plain-text mode buffers stdout until the model finishes — so all AssistantText events arrive in one burst at end of run instead of streaming.\n\nThe fix is to switch claude argv to `--output-format stream-json --verbose` and rewrite the parser to decode NDJSON envelopes. Each stdout line becomes one JSON object. Dispatch by `type` field:\n- `system.*` → swallow (init + hook chrome)\n- `assistant.message.content[*]` of type `text` → emit `AssistantText{Text: ...}`\n- `assistant.message.content[*]` of type `tool_use` → emit `ToolCall{Name: name, Args: JSON(input)}`\n- `assistant.message.content[*]` of type `thinking` → swallow\n- `user.*` (tool_result echoes) → swallow\n- `rate_limit_event` → swallow\n- `result` → final `Tokens{In: input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens + cache_creation_input_tokens, Out: output_tokens}` then `Finished{Success: !is_error}`\n\nThe relevant files:\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go` — modify `buildReviewCmd` argv, rewrite `parseClaudeOutput`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go` — replace `TestReviewer_EventStream` with `TestParseClaudeOutput_DecodesStreamJSON`, update `TestReviewer_ArgvShape`, drop `TestParseClaudeOutput_StreamsPerLine`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/canned_session.txt` — delete (old plain-text fixture)\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_session.jsonl` — new JSONL fixture\n\nA pre-captured JSONL fixture is at `/tmp/streaming-fixtures/claude-stream.jsonl` — copy it into `testdata/`.\n\nConstraints:\n- Do NOT touch codex, gemini-cli, the template (`cmd/entire/cli/review/types/template.go`), or `cmd/entire/cli/review/{run,run_multi,tui_*}.go`.\n- Do NOT add PTY anything (a previous attempt was reverted).\n- Do NOT change the `AgentReviewer` interface.\n- The helper `collectEvents` is already defined at the bottom of `reviewer_test.go` — REUSE it; do NOT redeclare.\n\nExisting event types from `cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go`:\n```go\ntype Event interface{ isEvent() }\ntype Started struct{}\ntype AssistantText struct{ Text string }\ntype ToolCall struct{ Name string; Args string }\ntype Tokens struct{ In int; Out int }\ntype Finished struct{ Success bool }\ntype RunError struct{ Err error }\n```\n\n## Tasks (do in order, end with one commit)\n\n### Task 1 — Capture fixture\n\nCopy `/tmp/streaming-fixtures/claude-stream.jsonl` to `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_session.jsonl`. Verify it's valid NDJSON.\n\n### Task 2 — Write failing fixture test\n\nAdd this test to `reviewer_test.go` (alongside the existing tests, before `collectEvents`):\n\n```go\nfunc TestParseClaudeOutput_DecodesStreamJSON(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    data, err := os.ReadFile(\"testdata/stream_session.jsonl\")\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"read fixture: %v\", err)\n    }\n    events := collectEvents(parseClaudeOutput(strings.NewReader(string(data))))\n\n    if _, ok := events[0].(reviewtypes.Started); !ok {\n        t.Errorf(\"events[0] = %T, want Started\", events[0])\n    }\n    last := events[len(events)-1]\n